export function inspectAstrometry(rows:readonly AstrometryRow[]){if(!rows.length)throw new TypeError('Astrometry needs rows.');const ids=new Set<string>();for(const row of rows){stable(row.id,'astrometry row id');if(ids.has(row.id))throw new TypeError(`Duplicate astrometry row ${row.id}.`);ids.add(row.id);finite(row.raDeg,'right ascension');finite(row.decDeg,'declination');if(row.raDeg<0||row.raDeg>=360||row.decDeg< -90||row.decDeg>90)throw new TypeError('Astrometry coordinates are outside their angular domain.');for(const [key,value] of Object.entries(row))if(typeof value==='number')finite(value,key);for(const [index,value] of (row.covariance??[]).entries())finite(value,`covariance ${index}`);}const covarianceLengths=new Set(rows.flatMap(row=>row.covariance?[row.covariance.length]:[]));if(covarianceLengths.size>1||covarianceLengths.has(0))throw new TypeError('Astrometric covariance shapes must be nonempty and consistent.');return{rows:rows.length,hasProperMotion:rows.every(row=>row.pmRaCosDecMasYr!==undefined&&row.pmDecMasYr!==undefined),hasParallax:rows.some(row=>row.parallaxMas!==undefined),hasRadialVelocity:rows.every(row=>row.radialVelocityKmS!==undefined),hasCovariance:rows.every(row=>row.covariance!==undefined),covarianceLength:covarianceLengths.values().next().value as number|undefined};}
